## Verdict: HOLD

Default-on auto-update can seat a placeholder Grok reply as usable, roll back to an unknown version, splice unsanitised model ids into the roster, and expose API keys to installer scripts.

### Blockers

- **F03-1** `crates/c3/src/engines/grok.rs:707` - Grok placeholder reply becomes usable when a turn reads then emits no post-tool text: final_text is empty, so the whole-stream text (the pre-read placeholder) is used and ok=true, bypassing the zero-tool guard because tool_calls>0. Verify: Unit-test read_grok_events/grok_turn_outcome with that stream; expect not ok and no usable reply. Remedy: When tool_calls>0 and final_text is blank, fail the turn (empty final answer) instead of falling back to whole-stream text; keep whole text only as salvage.

### Unproven scenarios

- A real engine update, rollback, kimi installer run and roster swap have never been exercised live (stated in the brief).
- The full c3-cli integration suite has not completed: its first pass stopped on a claude --version preflight timeout under load.
- Whether z.ai returns more than one TOKENS_LIMIT item, and whether real roster plan slugs collide across vendors, was not verified against live responses.
- pid_alive behaviour with an empty start_time in a stale lock was not inspected in the liveness implementation.

### First-run checklist (observable)

- [ ] Watch the first detached pass end-to-end: lock appears once, state.json advances last_pass/next_due once, and the report is printed exactly once by a later hook.
- [ ] Before/after each engine update record --version, the smoke result and, on any post-update smoke failure, proof the re-read version equals the pre-update version.
- [ ] Diff the roster against its .bak-maintain-<date> backup: exactly one model value may differ, on the intended provider entry.
- [ ] Confirm no engine with a live consultation/process was updated and no swap was seated while its plan window was saturated.
- [ ] Check last-run.log and state for kimi/npm/grok child output containing no API-key values and no unexpected redirect host.

